---
title: "The Paper Lesson"
note: "Improper Bodies: the Curator shows paper logic on a harmless object first, then the body of VICTIM folds like living paper. Codie's Curator as a CAST member (Shizuka or Reiji roll from __curator__, and ratings learn which one works). VICTIM is your ref image 1; delete (image 1) for text only."
tags: [curator, h3, body_horror, ito]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$curator = __curator__
$victim = __bh_victim__
$room = __bh_room__
$touch = {chest|sternum|collarbone}

CAST
CURATOR: $curator
VICTIM (image 1): $victim

SHOT 10s | push in, small, slow
CURATOR stands calm and perfectly composed beside VICTIM in $room, a sheet of paper and a heavy ceramic mug on a small table between them. CURATOR lifts the mug and lets it fall once; it lands with a dull, ordinary thud.
CURATOR (soft, polite voice): __curator_line__
CURATOR folds the sheet of paper once with precise care, places it in the hands of VICTIM and lightly touches VICTIM on the $touch with two fingers. A sharp fold line appears down the center of the torso, and the body of VICTIM begins bending inward along it as though made of thick living paper, creasing into clean flat planes while VICTIM stays alive, conscious and horrified. The arms flatten and hinge at unnatural angles; the face stays intact and expressive while the head grows subtly flatter. In the final moment VICTIM settles into a partially folded upright shape, still visibly human, and CURATOR bends down to adjust one fold with great care.
SFX: quiet room ambience; calm footsteps; soft paper-folding creases across the body; strained breathing
MUSIC: N/A
